BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261018T170000Z
DTEND:20261018T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261018T000000Z
SUMMARY:An Homage to Home: A Workshop and Reading
DESCRIPTION:Spend an afternoon finding community as we explore the 
 questions: Where is your story of origin rooted? With whom? In an 
 all-skills level workshop meant for Richmonders affected by diaspora\, we 
 will dive into poetic storytelling using the practice of 
 ekphrasis—writing based on visual art. For the workshop\, please bring a 
 digital or physical copy of any visual art (photograph\, short video\, 
 painting\, etc.) that reminds you of your place of origin. And then stay 
 after the workshop for a reading featuring local writers and an open mic. 
 The workshop will be facilitated by Felix Salmoran and Fairouz Bsharat. 
 \n\nThe workshop will run from roughly 1:00 pm - 3:00 pm and the reading 
 will run from roughly 3:15 pm - 4:30 pm. Please register and indicate 
 whether you are interested in the workshop\, reading\, or both!
LOCATION:Auditorium - Main Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Ben Himmelfarb":MAILTO:benjamin.himmelfarb@richmondgov.com
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks, Workshops
UID:LibCal-7469-17051656
URL:https://rvalibrary.libcal.com/event/17051656
END:VEVENT
